          "title": "You'll want to know: कुम्भकारः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कुम्भकारः — kumbhakāraḥ — \"a potter\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "kumbhakāra is a compound of kumbha, \"pot\", which you have already met, and kāra, \"maker\", from the root √kṛ (MW). It lives on as Hindi kumhār, \"potter\" (CDIAL 3310)."
            }
          ]
